# The full oracle for inc-2sv, on a character generated from scratch. Read the
# result with tools/check_target_enter.sh; this file only plays the session.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/target-enter-stair.keys 1
#
# THE SCENE, WHICH NEEDS NO SAVE. A standard orc barbarian (chargen.keys) is
# placed ON the cave entrance -- the up staircase to the inn -- the moment he
# enters level 1. The '@' glyph hides the '<' underneath; step one square east
# and the '<' appears in the square he just left, which is how this session
# proves the spawn really was a stair. He also starts with Potions of Cure
# Disease, so the exact item Brian first reported is in the pack from turn one.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. The scene is validated and the #187 guard is exercised BEFORE
# the quaff, because on an unfixed build the quaff's target prompt never closes
# -- it swallows every keystroke after it. Everything that must run has to run
# first; the quaff, the one measurement that hangs when it fails, goes last.
#
# THREE THINGS ARE MEASURED:
#
#   1. THE SCENE IS REAL. He steps one square east. The vacated spawn square
#      renders '<' immediately west of '@'. A seed that spawned him off a stair
#      would lack this adjacency, and the check refuses to judge.
#
#   2. THE #187 GUARD SURVIVES. Standing now on Floor, he opens the 'y' menu,
#      chooses [u] Enter, and confirms the default self-target. Floor is not an
#      enterable portal, so the Enter verb must refuse, "You can't go in
#      anything here", from its new home in Player::YuseMenu.
#
#   3. THE BUG IS FIXED. He steps back west onto the staircase and quaffs a
#      Potion of Cure Disease (Q_TAR|Q_NEAR). The target prompt opens on
#      himself, on the stair; he presses ENTER. Before the fix the shared
#      prompt read this as "walk into the stair", refused it silently, and the
#      prompt stayed open (screen mode 9) with no turn spent. After the fix the
#      target is accepted, the potion is drunk, a turn passes and the game
#      returns to play (screen mode 2). That mode-2-and-a-turn is the oracle.

@include chargen.keys

# A turn to let the level settle, and a stamp to measure the quaff against.
.*1
@dump:before

# 1. THE SCENE IS REAL: step east, uncovering the '<' on the spawn square.
RIGHT
@dump:stepped

# 2. THE #187 GUARD: Enter a non-portal (self, now on Floor) must be refused.
y
u
@dump:enter-prompt
ENTER
@dump:after-enter

# 3. THE BUG: step back onto the stair, quaff, confirm the self-target on it.
LEFT
@dump:back-on-stair
q
@choose "3 Potions of Cure Disease"
@dump:target-prompt
ENTER
@dump:after-quaff

ESC
@quit
